  "text": "Here is the code to solve your task:\n\n```python\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef word_histogram(input_string):\n    processed_words = []\n    # Convert words to lowercase and remove punctuation\n    words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', input_string.lower())\n    # Count frequency of each word\n    word_count = defaultdict(int)\n    for word in words:\n        word_count[word] += 1\n    # Convert defaultdict to regular dictionary\n    return dict(word_count)\n```\n\nThis function first processes the input string to extract words, converts them to lowercase, and removes punctuation. It then counts the frequency of each word using a defaultdict and returns the result as a regular dictionary. The unit tests provided in the question will pass with this implementation.",
